## LB-046: CL-049 KKT Support Rule

For the unequal-low one-drought LP in LB-044, let \((\alpha,\beta)\) be dual weights on low horizons and the final high, with \(\sum_j\alpha_j+\beta=1\). Define
\[
W_i(c)=\sum_{\substack{j>i\\ c\le m_{i,j}}}\alpha_j
\]
and
\[
\psi_i=
\left[
\max_{c\in\mathcal L}
\left\{
cW_i(c)-\beta(h-c)
\right\}
\right]_+.
\]
Then complementary slackness gives the support rule
\[
x_{i,c}>0
\quad\Longrightarrow\quad
cW_i(c)-\beta(h-c)=\psi_i.
\]
If \(\psi_i=0\), positive mass can appear only at levels satisfying
\[
cW_i(c)=\beta(h-c);
\]
if the raw maximum is negative, no positive \(x_{i,c}\) can appear on that segment. Capacity binding is not equivalent to \(\psi_i>0\): a segment capacity may bind while \(\psi_i=0\).

Status: accepted as a direct LP complementary-slackness consequence of LB-044, not as a pooling algorithm. It is the right starting point for active-set or nested-allocation attempts, which must still output both primal masses and dual weights.

Regression certificate from iteration 19. For
\[
